<ns0:problem id="fs-id1167836507876">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836507878">The number of unread emails in Bryan’s account is 100. This number grows by 15 unread emails a day. The function <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>=</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>100</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>+</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>15</ns1:mn><ns1:mi>t</ns1:mi></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> represents the relation between the number of emails, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">N</ns0:emphasis>, and the time, <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">t</ns0:emphasis>, measured in days.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836360895"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> Determine the independent and dependent variable.</ns0:para>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167829619314"><ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> Find <ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>N</ns1:mi><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mn>7</ns1:mn><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> Explain what this result means.</ns0:para>
</ns0:problem>
<ns0:solution id="fs-id1167836622270">
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167836622272"><ns0:span class="token">ⓐ</ns0:span> <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">t</ns0:emphasis> IND; <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">N</ns0:emphasis> DEP <ns0:span class="token">ⓑ</ns0:span> 205; the number of unread emails in Bryan’s account on the seventh day.</ns0:para>
</ns0:solution>
</ns0:exercise>
